  "final": "I moved the duplicated parsing into a new top-level module, `common_dates.py`. It holds one `FORMATS` tuple and one `parse_date(value, label)` function. The four existing tests pass, including the one that checks the error wording.\n\n- **`schedule/dates.py`:** `parse_due_date` now just calls `parse_date(text, \"due date\")`.\n- **`reports/dates.py`:** `parse_report_date` now just calls `parse_date(value, \"report date\")`.\n\nBoth keep their public names and signatures, so `planner.py` and `summary.py` are untouched. Errors still read `unrecognised due date: ...` and `unrecognised report date: ...`.\n\nThe old `reports.dates.FORMATS` constant is gone from that module. Nothing in the repo used it, but anything outside the repo importing it would break. The new module's `FORMATS` is the same tuple.\n\nI put `common_dates.py` at the repo root because the repo has no shared package. If you'd rather it live somewhere like `utils/`, that's an easy move.",
